web: let the web worker extension host's iframe take its origin from a `webEndpointUrlTemplate` that does not name a quality

The web workbench runs the web worker extension host (browser-only extensions) in an iframe. With `webEndpointUrlTemplate` in the
product configuration the iframe gets an origin of its own (`{{uuid}}` = `v--` + a hash of the page's origin and a stable salt,
checked again by the iframe's page), as vscode.dev does; without it the iframe has the page's own origin. The template is used only
when the product has both a commit AND a quality, even when the template names neither, so a build without a quality (Code - OSS,
whose product.json has none) cannot give the host an origin of its own at all. The webview endpoint, built from the same kind of
template, has no such condition (environmentService.webviewExternalEndpoint).

This uses the template when it does not contain `{{quality}}` even if the product has no quality. A template that names the quality, and
every product that has one, behave as before. An embedder whose page cannot or should not frame its own origin (such as a vmapp
window: `frame-src` admits only isolated `vmapp-frame://` origins) can then give the host an isolated origin by an embedder
`productConfiguration.webEndpointUrlTemplate`, without claiming a quality it does not have (the quality changes many defaults).

--- a/src/vs/workbench/services/extensions/browser/webWorkerExtensionHost.ts
+++ b/src/vs/workbench/services/extensions/browser/webWorkerExtensionHost.ts
@@ -96,18 +96,20 @@
 			const webEndpointUrlTemplate = this._productService.webEndpointUrlTemplate;
 			const commit = this._productService.commit;
 			const quality = this._productService.quality;
-			if (webEndpointUrlTemplate && commit && quality) {
+			// A template that does not name the quality needs none (a build without a quality, such as Code - OSS, can still give the
+			// iframe an origin of its own)
+			if (webEndpointUrlTemplate && commit && (quality || !webEndpointUrlTemplate.includes('{{quality}}'))) {
 				// Try to keep the web worker extension host iframe origin stable by storing it in workspace storage
 				const key = 'webWorkerExtensionHostIframeStableOriginUUID';
 				let stableOriginUUID = this._storageService.get(key, StorageScope.WORKSPACE);
 				if (typeof stableOriginUUID === 'undefined') {
 					stableOriginUUID = generateUuid();
 					this._storageService.store(key, stableOriginUUID, StorageScope.WORKSPACE, StorageTarget.MACHINE);
 				}
 				const hash = await parentOriginHash(mainWindow.origin, stableOriginUUID);
 				const baseUrl = (
 					webEndpointUrlTemplate
 						.replace('{{uuid}}', `v--${hash}`) // using `v--` as a marker to require `parentOrigin`/`salt` verification
 						.replace('{{commit}}', commit)
-						.replace('{{quality}}', quality)
+						.replace('{{quality}}', quality ?? '')
 				);

